comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-13T07:57:00.458Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation evidence (2026-11-13): TOON-only presentation rule in renderToonOmissionReceipt/projectDerivableOmissionReceipt (src/core/output/output.ts). When every omitted group is exactly {name, restore_with} and restore_with is one shared prefix plus the name, TOON prints omitted_field_groups[N] as an inline name list plus one restore_with template ending in <name>, and only when that is smaller. Any non-derivable hint or extra row field keeps the per-row form; pm get's children/dependency_provenance receipt keeps its table. JSON, SDK and MCP keep the typed per-row receipt because complete-list.ts, list-envelope.ts and read-output-budget.ts read omitted_field_groups[].restore_with. Measured on a fresh tracker: default pm context receipt 505 -> 265 B (whole read 1,322 -> 1,082 B); JSON unchanged at 2,542 B by design. has_omissions and omitted_field_group_count stay so the receipt keeps its contract keys."
